WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.809
Zack Snyder's zombie-verse is alive and kicking
in the prequel movie Army of Thieves, giving

00:00:05.809 --> 00:00:10.430
us a stack of secret clues that could well
prove my crazy time loop theory.

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:14.531
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining everything that

00:00:14.531 --> 00:00:19.300
Army of Thieves reveals about the future of
the Army of the Dead franchise and some huge

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.090
updates for Snyder's sequel Planet of the
Dead.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.470
Spoilers ahead, of course, for both movies.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:28.169
I first mentioned the serious probability
that the team in Army of the Dead were stuck

00:00:28.169 --> 00:00:31.509
in a strange kind of time loop in my video
about that movie.

00:00:31.509 --> 00:00:36.050
The key moment happens in the casino basement
when the group come across some skeletons.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:37.379
There's another team of grave robbers.

00:00:37.379 --> 00:00:39.540
Is it another team, or is it us, Dieter?

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:40.740
I mean, look at them.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.740
It's us.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.039
The skeletons are uncannily wearing almost
identical clothes, from Peters' Hawaiian shirt

00:00:46.039 --> 00:00:47.640
to Scott's red bandana.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.989
Zack Snyder has since confirmed he deliberately
asked the production team to make the skeletons

00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:56.790
look like the crew and that the dried-up bodies
around the second set of plans the team find

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:00.170
on the casino floor are meant to be versions
of them as well.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:04.320
And now Army of Thieves has laid out its own
set of clues which support my Army of the

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.890
Dead time loop theory.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:10.510
The first comes when Dieter introduces the
story of Hans Wagner, a master locksmith who

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:15.270
designed four extremely-difficult-to-crack
safes, each one named after an opera from

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:17.380
Richard Wagner's epic Ring Cycle.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.020
Das Rheingold
The Valkyrie

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.230
The Siegfried
And the Götterdämmerung.

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:25.450
The Götterdämmerung is the safe the crew
break into in Vegas, and the first three safes

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:28.130
are the ones Dieter cracks in Army of Thieves.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:32.120
The fact the new movie establishes that the
Götterdämmerung is both the fourth safe

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:36.600
and the fourth work in Wagner's epic opera
is an important detail as there are clues

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.320
that the time loop we see in Army of the Dead
may be on its fourth iteration.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.110
For example, the necklace that Cruz wears
in the movie has four holes, whereas the same

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.760
necklace on her skeleton only has three.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:52.630
Originally, the nuke was due to hit Vegas
on the Fourth of July and the Liberace impersonator

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.670
counts to four as the zombie apocalypse kicks
off in Vegas.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:02:01.210
And the convoy transporting Zeus out of Area
51 refer to themselves as the Four Horsemen.

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:06.110
Vanderohe's repetition of "fighting and dying"
three times could also imply there have been

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:07.840
three previous time loops.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:14.490
We're caught in some infinite loop of fighting
and dying, fighting and dying, fighting and

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:15.490
dying.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:18.120
And Dieter thinks he shot the zombie bride
three times when it was actually four:

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:19.410
I shot her three times.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.450
Actually, it was four.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:24.780
It's strange that Dieter should get this wrong,
and could imply he's misremembering how he

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.450
shot her three times on the previous loop.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:31.900
By the way, in Army of Thieves there's a neat
easter egg to that kill when Dieter sees a

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:37.810
news report about the Vegas outbreak and there's
a zombie bride shuffling around in the background.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:42.150
Also in Army of Thieves, as Dieter is figuring
out how to crack the Valkyrie safe he says...

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:46.990
I believe the locks are to be solved in the
order of the story and then the cycle begins

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:49.090
anew.
...which could suggest that cracking all of

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:53.880
Wagner's four safes will kick off a new cycle
or time loop, if you like.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:58.780
Finally, in some mind-bending, ironic reveal...
it all begins again.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:03.569
This idea is reinforced even further when
the Army of Thieves epilogue replays Scott

00:03:03.569 --> 00:03:08.180
and Cruz meeting Dieter for the first time,
and he comments about the prospect of cracking

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.650
Wagner's fourth [and final] safe.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:14.490
It's a doorway to another realm, my friends
and providence has brought you to me.

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:15.490
We go through it together.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:20.100
The idea that unlocking the Götterdämmerung
will be like opening a portal to another dimension

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:25.360
or timeline is implied after Dieter pushes
Vanderohe into the safe and shuts him in.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.370
So, when Vanderohe emerges in the aftermath
of the nuclear strike on Vegas and discovers

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:34.590
he's been bitten, this might be a completely
different timeline because we never saw Zeus

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:37.610
actually bite him before he went in the safe.

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:42.590
Now, as Dieter closed the door on Vanderohe,
his own fate was seemingly sealed as Zeus

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.900
pulled him away;
however, Army of Thieves has a tease to the

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:50.730
fan theory that Dieter actually survived given
that we never saw his death on screen.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.530
When Dieter cracks the first safe, he exclaims...

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:54.580
I'm invincible!

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.160
Okay, Mr. Invincible.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:01.600
This specific word choice implies that Dieter
survives his encounter with Alpha zombie Zeus,

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.650
or at least that he did in an alternate timeline.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:09.700
Of course, it could just be some ironic foreshadowing
of his death, but when discussing Dieter's

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:13.220
fate on a live-stream with TheFilmJunkee,
Snyder said that

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:16.380
"by the rules of horror...
if we don't see a character die"

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.439
that means the character can always return.

00:04:19.439 --> 00:04:23.169
Snyder has also just revealed that the title
of the Army of the Dead sequel will be Planet

00:04:23.169 --> 00:04:27.340
of the Dead and heavily implied that Dieter
survived and will be returning for the follow-up

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:28.340
movie.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:32.309
He also explained what we can expect from
Dieter in the sequel, and just before we get

00:04:32.309 --> 00:04:38.059
into that, some deadly cool easter eggs, I
want to thank the sponsor of this video, Trade.

